
# .cursor/rules/api-rest.mdc

## Rule: API Naming
- Follow RESTful naming conventions: nouns, plural form (e.g., /users, /products).
- Use route attributes instead of relying solely on naming conventions when required.

## Rule: HTTP Verbs
- Use [HttpGet], [HttpPost], [HttpPut], [HttpDelete] explicitly for endpoints.
- Do not mix responsibilities in the same method.

## Rule: Consistent Response Format
- Return IActionResult or ActionResult<T> consistently.
- Use Ok(), NotFound(), BadRequest(), etc. instead of raw return statements.

## Rule: Versioning
- If API versioning is used, preserve the version in the controller route (e.g., [Route("api/v1/[controller]")]).
